  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5361",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is linked to CAL-85-1 through a series of molecular interactions involving purinoceptors and a common chemical compound. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin targets P2X purinoceptor 1, which is subsequently targeted by [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, a compound that also targets CAL-85-1. Similarly, doxorubicin is associated with NCI-H46, which is also targeted by the same compound, reinforcing the connection between doxorubicin and CAL-85-1. The shared mechanism of targeting a common chemical entity, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, suggests a potential pathway where doxorubicin may act through this compound to influence CAL-85-1. The evidence supports a direct relationship between doxorubicin and CAL-85-1 via this shared target, highlighting the importance of the compound in mediating the interaction.",
